<title>JAPAN: IBJ says to leave Feb prime rate steady at 2.5 pct.</title>
<headline>IBJ says to leave Feb prime rate steady at 2.5 pct.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Industrial Bank of Japan Ltd said on Wednesday that it would leave its long-term prime lending rate unchanged at 2.5 percent for February from the previous month.  </p>
<p>The other two Japanese credit banks -- The Long-Term Credit Bank of Japan Ltd and Nippon Credit Bank Ltd -- have said they would announce their prime lending rates for February and terms for their new five-year debentures on Thursday.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-33432-8570</p>
</text>
